WEBVTT

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.480
<i>Previously on Foreman's One-Day Excursion!</i>

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.510
<i>The foreman of Team C, Odagiri,</i>

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:15.740
<i>started running a movie 
business in the underground.</i>

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:19.270
<i>Ootsuki, feeling threatened 
by its popularity,</i>

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.250
<i>arranged to accompany his next excursion...</i>

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:24.500
<i>while feigning coincidence!</i>

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.010
After you download your movies...

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:36.360
We could have a few drinks. My treat.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:50.150
<b><i>1-Day Excursion
Foreman</i></b>

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:15.780
<i>Agenda 22
</i><b>\h\h\h\h\h\h\hConclusions</b>

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:21.000
Ootsuki!

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:24.700
The downloads took longer than I expected...

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:25.490
Did you wait long?

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:28.500
Oh, not at all. Come on, let's go.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:37.880
<b>Miyuki</b>

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.570
Miyuki's Casual Dining?

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:42.390
Let's head on in.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:44.310
Hang on!

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:50.190
My instinct is telling me we 
should probably go elsewhere.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:52.030
What makes you say that?

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:53.190
Can't you tell?

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:58.570
From the style and name 
of it, this restaurant...

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:04.330
is probably a diner with a small 
group of tightly-knit regulars.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:07.080
Maybe I should marry her, then!

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.490
Oh, cut it out!

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:13.250
You can already hear the 
intimate-sounding laughter from inside.

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:16.140
This isn't the kind of place some 
underground laborers could just—

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:19.170
Come on, now, it'll be perfectly fine.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:21.590
Hey!

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:23.340
Welcome!

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:32.850
<i>For all his big talk, it played 
out just the way I imagined.</i>

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:36.860
<i>This guy isn't used to the outside.</i>

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:41.360
<i>He might be trying to look casual 
enough, but it's obvious. After all...</i>

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:45.750
<i>He hasn't let go of my 
sweater this entire time!</i>

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:51.010
<i>To save up for movies, he probably hasn't 
been using the one-day pass at all,</i>

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:56.000
<i>or maybe it's that he's spent all his 
time and money on downloads when he has?</i>

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.770
<i>He might be a fierce foe underground,</i>

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.690
<i>but up here, he's a harmless schoolgirl.</i>

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:08.260
<i>This version of Odagiri...</i>

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:14.760
<i>will provide no challenge when I 
swindle him out of the movie business!</i>

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:19.400
Huh... Ootsuki-san?

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:20.770
Hey there.

00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:23.290
It really is you!

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:26.160
It's been a while, ma'am.

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:29.300
Do you still have my bottle of shochu?

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:30.740
Sure do.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:33.410
Here you go.

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:37.290
You have a bottle here? 
When you're working underground?!

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:40.960
Huh? This is from my last visit.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.620
Is something weird about that?

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:43.220
No...

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:46.090
What can I get for your friend?

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:51.430
<b>Shochu

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:52.090
Uh...

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:57.190
<b>Menu</b>

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:57.190
Ootsuki, do you have any recommendations?

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:03.440
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:03.440
Wh-What is that?

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:06.420
Oh, nothing special.

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:09.980
I'm just toasting some salmon 
jerky with my lighter.

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:11.810
Here. Eat it while it's hot.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:13.450
Huh? Can I?

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:18.570
Here's some shochu cut with 
water to wash it down.

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:23.090
<b>Pwah!</b>

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:25.160
That goes really well with it!

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.380
It begins!

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:31.450
<i>It begins! Ootsuki's class 
on enjoying adult beverages!</i>

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:28.760
Ootsuki's class

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:31.100
on enjoying adult beverages

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:36.680
Go right ahead and take what 
you want. It's all delicious.

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:39.900
Th-Then I'll try the amberjack sashimi...

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:47.530
It's so plump!

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:49.660
At this time of year,

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:53.000
amberjack has a lot of fat, which keeps 
the soy sauce from being absorbed.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.720
So it's actually lightly scored.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:01.340
That kind of laborious touch isn't what 
you'd get from your typical place.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:03.460
Thanks for the praise.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:06.970
I get it...

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:15.060
Stop!

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:19.730
For the last piece, let's dip it in the pot...

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:22.220
for improvised amberjack shabu-shabu.

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:38.570
I get it!

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:39.750
See, see?

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.250
Drink up, drink up!

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:50.260
<i>Between the owner's comforting cuisine 
and Ootsuki's strange reassurances...</i>

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:54.390
<i>This diner, which first seemed 
like hostile territory,</i>

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:57.240
<i>now holds an incredible amount of enjoyment!</i>

00:06:57.890 --> 00:07:00.980
<i>From anxiety to pleasure!</i>

00:06:57.890 --> 00:07:03.060
<b>From anxiety to pleasure...!</b>

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:07.410
<i>And naturally, the drinks begin to flow.</i>

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:14.160
<i>The usually cautious Odagiri finds himself
completely drunk before long!</i>

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:18.160
<i>This was too easy.</i>

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:21.290
<i>And so, several minutes later,</i>

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:24.420
<i>even their designated overseer, 
Miyamoto, joins in the fun.</i>

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:27.420
<i>And the conversation takes 
a turn for the lively!</i>

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.670
Wait, you like yoga, Miyamoto-san?

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:32.950
You bet I do! I love it!

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:39.460
<i>It's about time...</i>

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.190
Amberjack and daikon.

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:45.560
What about them? You want to eat some?

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:47.370
Here.

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:48.800
Oh, no...

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.580
I was just thinking

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:54.820
about how you and I are a lot like 
the amberjack with daikon radish.

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:58.120
I'm the daikon, and you're the amberjack.

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:01.080
Individually, we're plenty tasty,

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:05.570
but when we're together, 
we push each other even further.

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:07.880
It's a win-win relationship.

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:10.230
What do you think?

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:15.840
Your cinema and my chinchiro games... 
Suppose we combine the two!

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:25.850
<b>EC Land</b>

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:18.640
We'll create the greatest entertainment space

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:21.000
in the underground where 
people can enjoy both!

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:25.850
Why don't we make EC Land happen?

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:27.860
EC...

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:33.350
<i>That's right. What I want is a merger 
and acquisition with Team C.</i>

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:39.320
<i>And from that, in time...</i>

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:46.250
<i>I will take over the movie business!</i>

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:51.380
<i>The normal Odagiri would 
never bite at such an offer,</i>

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:53.620
<i>but now that he's drunk...</i>

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:04.640
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:04.640
<i>Damn! Did I speak too soon?</i>

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:07.830
Well, I'm just talking about hypotheticals.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:08.870
A card...

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:11.900
One that works for both 
Team E and C's businesses...

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:15.770
We'll call it an EC Point stamp card.

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:21.290
<i>He took the bait!</i>

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:22.960
That sounds fantastic!

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:24.060
Right?! Doesn't it?!

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:25.310
<b>He's in...!</b>

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:25.720
<i>He's in!</i>

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:29.860
We can do stuff like half off a bag of snack 
mix with the purchase of a movie ticket!

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:31.790
That's downright diabolical!

00:09:31.790 --> 00:09:33.320
How about a gambling film festival?

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:34.860
I love it! I absolutely love it!

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:37.750
Oh, we <i>have</i> to start working together!

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:40.800
You ready to do this?

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:42.560
<i>It's done!</i>

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:46.040
<i>I've got a verbal commitment!</i>

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:46.810
<b>Verbal Commitment</b>

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:49.400
<i>Wait... I can't relax yet.</i>

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:51.820
<i>I still need to be careful.</i>

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:53.620
Miyamoto-san.

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:59.650
Would you act as the witness for 
this deal between Teams C and E?

00:09:59.650 --> 00:10:00.670
Who, me?

00:10:00.670 --> 00:10:01.700
Yeah!

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.510
Okay, fair enough.

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:07.670
Then how about you two make 
it official over this cup?

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:08.970
Good idea!

00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:10.740
Well, then...

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:16.690
You, too, Odagiri-san.

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:20.070
Odagiri-san? Something wrong?

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:23.100
Well, this was just 
reminding me of something.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:27.100
There's a scene in <i>Once Upon 
a Time in America</i> like this.

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:33.690
Oh, yeah, there was a scene like 
this in <i>Once Upon a Time in America</i>!

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:34.680
Right?

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:37.360
There really was, wasn't there, Ootsuki?

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:39.940
Uh, well...

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:42.240
I haven't seen that one yet.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.700
You're kidding... You've never seen it?

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:48.740
<i>Once Upon a Time in America</i>?

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:50.250
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:51.850
Well... er...

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:53.260
You gotta be kidding me!

00:10:53.260 --> 00:10:56.630
It's a classic! And you've never 
seen <i>Once Upon a Time in America</i>?

00:10:56.630 --> 00:11:04.260
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:10:57.160 --> 00:11:00.260
Well, putting that aside...

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:04.260
<i>Damned obnoxious film geeks!</i>

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:10.140
Ootsuki-san, you should really 
see <i>Once Upon a Time in America</i>!

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:12.950
What?! You, too?

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:15.680
Well, I'll check it out sometime...

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:16.270
Nope!

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:19.400
Not "sometime"! Right now!

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:20.440
I've got it.

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:25.990
It's loaded on here. 
<i>Once Upon a Time in America</i>.

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:34.250
<i>I'd really rather have the 
drink to seal the deal...</i>

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:36.540
We don't have to watch 
it right now, do we?

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:38.340
We do! Right now!

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:44.180
<i>Well... we've got three 
hours until the time limit,</i>

00:11:44.610 --> 00:11:46.390
<i>so I guess when the movie's over...</i>

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:47.890
<b>But</b>

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:47.890
<i>But!</i>

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:50.010
<i>It turns out to be the extended cut</i>

00:11:50.010 --> 00:11:54.200
<i>of </i>Once Upon a Time in America<i>, with a 
run time of 3 hours and 50 minutes!</i>

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:58.900
Time's up, Ootsuki, Odagiri.

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:03.660
<i>And he's definitively out of time!</i>

00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:11.910
<b>No M&A!</b>

00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:11.910
<i>There will be no merge and 
acquisition this time!</i>

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:15.920
It's too damn long! 
Both the title and the run time!

00:12:16.890 --> 00:12:19.700
<i>Despite being in the hellish underworld 
that is underground prison,</i>

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:22.610
<i>he seeks to enjoy his one-day 
excursions to their utmost.</i>

00:12:22.610 --> 00:12:25.930
<i>From the bottom, he seeks the top!</i>

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:31.210
<i>Where will Foreman Ootsuki's 
next one-day pass take him?</i>

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:36.540
About that merger and acquisition...

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:37.940
Not happening.

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:42.280
<i>Previously on </i>Mr. Tonegawa's 
Middle Management Blues<i>...</i>

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:48.580
<i>Tonegawa took over for Nakata as the man 
behind Teiai's official Twitter account.</i>

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:52.000
<i>However! His follower count 
doesn't grow as expect,</i>

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:56.460
<i>with a hate account by an experienced 
Twitterer outdoing him.</i>

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:59.090
<i>And then a new fact came to light...</i>

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:03.240
The specific contents of the soup

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:06.470
are something that no one 
from the outside could know.

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:08.090
<b>Psst...</b>

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:11.470
Which means these hate posts...

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:14.230
are coming from someone inside the company!

00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:23.940
<i>Someone here... is the culprit!</i>

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:28.740
<b>Meeting Room 3</b>

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:28.740
<i>An emergency meeting is 
called for Team Tonegawa.</i>

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:34.260
Well, this hate account now 
has over 7,000 followers,

00:13:34.260 --> 00:13:37.130
with its influence spreading by the day.

00:13:37.130 --> 00:13:42.630
Not only that, but there's a strong likelihood 
that it's run by someone who works for Teiai.

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:46.130
<b>Psst...</b>

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:49.400
That being the case, if you 
see anything suspicious...

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:51.960
What is it, Saemon?

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:55.790
Well... there was a new 
post by the hate account.

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:56.920
Show me.

00:13:57.770 --> 00:14:04.280
The old dude in the two-piece tweed suits
ought to remember his employees'
names by now.

00:13:58.330 --> 00:14:00.650
"The old dude in the two-piece tweed suits

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:04.280
ought to remember his 
employees' names by now."

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:08.780
Who's this "old dude in 
the two-piece tweed suit"?

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:11.780
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:13.530
It couldn't be anyone else...

00:14:13.970 --> 00:14:17.180
I'm fairly sure it's you, Tonegawa-sensei.

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:18.790
What? Me?

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:21.790
<b>Yep... Yep...</b>

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:23.090
Me?

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:23.570
<b>Yep... Yep...</b>

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:25.250
This is strange.

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:30.140
This isn't something just 
anyone in Teiai would know...

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:34.510
It'd have to be a man in black 
assigned to Team Tonegawa.

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:39.930
<i>And thus the list of suspects is narrowed.</i>

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:43.290
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:14:44.210 --> 00:14:47.610
Now, hold on a second, Tonegawa-sensei!

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:51.650
There's no way one of us is a traitor!

00:14:51.650 --> 00:14:53.620
This is crazy!

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:54.870
Stop.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:58.730
Where do you think you're 
going, Doushita-san?

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:00.650
You little...

00:15:00.650 --> 00:15:01.880
Give it a rest!

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:04.370
<i>With a single tweet...</i>

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.630
<b>Doubt & Suspicion</b>

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:06.630
<i>Doubt and suspicion are sown.</i>

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:10.890
<i>And an edgy atmosphere envelops the team.</i>

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:15.390
<b>Edgy... Edgy... Edgy...</b>

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:21.520
<i>And then, as if to laugh 
at Tonegawa's suffering...</i>

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:23.560
You go out for coffee and a business meeting.
You have to pay for it all.
Yes. That's Teiai.

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:24.160
<i>The hate account continues to tweet,</i>

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:26.520
I danced the Teiai dance.

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:26.520
<i>with its follower count finally reaching...</i>

00:15:26.520 --> 00:15:29.780
<b>Followers</b>

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:29.780
<i>over 10,000 users!</i>

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:33.280
Damn it! I need to do something about this.

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:37.540
Tonegawa-sensei, did you find anything?

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:39.320
Oh, Saemon.

00:15:40.050 --> 00:15:46.140
No. I was trying to look through his tweets 
to see if there were any hints,

00:15:46.140 --> 00:15:48.050
but I couldn't find anything.

00:15:49.750 --> 00:15:52.300
Can you go back to that last tweet?

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:54.210
This one?

00:15:57.720 --> 00:16:01.310
<i>This angle... Just maybe...</i>

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:04.350
Excuse me, I need to use this for a second.

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:05.940
Did you figure something out?

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:09.320
Not exactly... But there's a chance...

00:16:10.310 --> 00:16:14.320
If we open this picture of a tablet 
in an image editing program...

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:15.880
Image

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:17.760
Image... Adjustments...

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:17.080
Mode

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:17.080
Adjustments

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:20.080
Brightness/Contrast

